-- separator_ids() -> every entity id that is a sequence separator rather than content.
--
-- ONE BODY FOR ONE TRUTH (§15). The category-name literals were previously typed
-- inline in corpus_whitespace_vocab_indices; a second call site copying them is the
-- divergence this law exists to prevent. Every caller resolves through here.
--
-- TWO TIERS, ONE RULE. A separator is an atom whose Unicode general category says
-- so, OR a grapheme cluster composed entirely of such atoms. The second arm is not
-- a special case: UAX#29 GB3 makes CR+LF a single grapheme, so the cluster is a
-- first-class entity at tier 1 and can never carry a category attestation of its
-- own -- categories are atom-level facts. Composition lifts the property (§3,
-- composition is Merkle), so bool_and over the constituents IS the definition.
--
-- Measured on the foundation substrate 2026-07-29: 84 atoms + 1 grapheme (CRLF)
-- = 85 ids, 1.2 s for the whole set. Bounded by the alphabet, not by the corpus --
-- the same class of lookup as relation_type_id(), and explicitly NOT a corpus
-- cache. Nothing here scans ingested content.
--
-- NO RENDER FALLBACK. An earlier shape reached for is_all_whitespace(render_text_
-- fast(...)) whenever a token had no category attestation. That was compensating
-- for the grapheme arm being missing, and it hid the reason: composites are
-- unattested BY CONSTRUCTION, not by incomplete seeding. Rendering to classify is
-- also the read-side law inverted -- classification is an indexed read on the id;
-- the render is the cost.
--
-- SCRIPT HONESTY: Zs/Zl/Zp/Cc are the Unicode separator and control categories.
-- For a script that does not delimit with separator characters (Han, Thai,
-- Japanese) the set is simply empty for its atoms and the sequence is
-- content-contiguous -- the correct answer, not a silent failure.
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION separator_ids()
    RETURNS bytea[]
    LANGUAGE sql STABLE
    SET search_path = @extschema@, public AS $$
    WITH atoms AS (
        SELECT DISTINCT a.subject_id AS id
        FROM attestations a
        JOIN canonical_names cn ON cn.id = a.object_id
        WHERE a.type_id = relation_type_id('HAS_GENERAL_CATEGORY')
          AND cn.name IN ('unicode/category/Zs/v1',
                          'unicode/category/Zl/v1',
                          'unicode/category/Zp/v1',
                          'unicode/category/Cc/v1')
    ),
    clusters AS (
        SELECT e.id
        FROM entities e
        JOIN v_word_points w ON w.id = e.id AND w.trajectory IS NOT NULL
        CROSS JOIN LATERAL public.laplace_trajectory_constituents(w.trajectory) c
        WHERE e.tier = 1
        GROUP BY e.id
        HAVING bool_and(c.entity_id IN (SELECT id FROM atoms))
    )
    SELECT array_agg(id) FROM (
        SELECT id FROM atoms
        UNION
        SELECT id FROM clusters
    ) s
$$;
